This product (v2.1.1) is a rewrite in Rust. Its behaviour is modelled on the
prior Python release v1.9.162 (the reference implementation); the current
per-area conformance status -- aligned, unverified, or known gaps -- is
documented in README.md ("Conformance status vs v1.9.162").

It bundles/links the following Rust crates (see Cargo.lock for the
exact versions and their respective licenses):

  tokio, futures, async-trait                       (MIT)
  axum, hyper, hyper-util, tower, tower-http        (MIT)
  tokio-tungstenite                                 (MIT/Apache-2.0)
  rustls, tokio-rustls, rustls-pemfile, webpki-roots
    (TLS provider: aws-lc-rs / ring as configured) (Apache-2.0/ISC/MIT)
  quinn                                             (Apache-2.0/MIT)
  serde, serde_json, bytes, thiserror, tracing,
    tracing-subscriber, clap, regex, once_cell, lru,
    dashmap, parking_lot, rand, hex, url,
    rust-embed, mime_guess, num_cpus, socket2, libc (MIT/Apache-2.0)
  idna                                              (MIT/Apache-2.0/Unicode-3.0)
  aya, aya-log, aya-build                           (MIT/Apache-2.0)
  criterion                                         (Apache-2.0/MIT)
  leptos, wasm-bindgen, gloo-net, gloo-timers       (MIT/Apache-2.0)

The WebAssembly frontend and the XDP eBPF program are built from the
same source tree.  DNS message encoding/decoding is an original
implementation written to match the behavior of this project's
Python reference; no third-party DNS resolver core is used.
